WEBVTT

00:00:01.630 --> 00:00:04.980
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the World Champion, Dande…

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:10.110
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew…

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:15.570
This is the story of their lives and adventures.

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:25.900
Isshu Region
Here we are!

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:27.670
The Isshu Region!
Isshu Region

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:28.210
The hottest spot in Isshu right now:
The Resort Desert!
Isshu Region

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:32.090
The hottest spot in Isshu right now:
The Resort Desert!

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:33.800
All right! There it is!

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:38.430
The newly-uncovered ruins;
The Ruins of the Titan!

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:41.390
Try your hand at solving
their ancient riddles!

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:44.380
That “Titan” has <i>got</i> to
be a Pokémon!

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:46.630
Yeah! I think so, too!

00:00:46.630 --> 00:00:50.440
Wait for me, Isshu Pokémon!

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:57.820
…So, how do we get there?

00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:00.200
I thought you’d worked that out…

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.150
Wait, you don’t have a plan?!

00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:03.460
You don’t, either!

00:01:07.490 --> 00:01:08.600
Pikachu!

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:12.840
This desert is way too hot!

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:17.330
Hibunny, you can take the heat?

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:20.010
That’s what being a Fire type
gets you, I guess.

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:28.230
How do we cross?

00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:33.570
Don’t underestimate
the Resort Desert, you two!

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:43.540
PocketMonsters

00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:45.960
Hey, you still not ready? C'mon, hurry up!

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:48.540
You all packed and ready to leave?

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:51.260
I'll show you this wide mysterious world

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:54.130
And skip the slow send-off

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:56.470
Be it through fire or through water

00:01:56.470 --> 00:01:59.140
I'm fumbling blindly through the days

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:03.640
When I don't even know what the next second will bring

00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:08.900
Each and every one of my memories

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:13.490
Can always be found inside a Ball

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:17.410
On 1, 2, 3, dive in!

00:02:17.410 --> 00:02:23.160
I've got the future plans I imagined in my pocket

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:30.170
Greeting someone new is always fresh

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:34.380
No need (No need!) to hesitate! Try! (Try!)

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:35.720
Let's have a fight!

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:38.430
1: Once the battle's done

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:40.260
2: And we're laughing or crying

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:44.600
On 3, let's be friends!

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:51.270
Any day and every day, that's always been my rule

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:56.610
With this unpredictable, boundless world awaiting

00:02:56.610 --> 00:02:59.110
Let's go! Every time you trip and fall

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:03.240
Let's go! You pick yourself up by my side

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:05.040
I choose you!

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:14.050
A Raid Battle in the Ruins!!
My First Time in the Isshu Region!

00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:17.880
Whoa, an Asanan!

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:19.970
Lucky you… I want one, too!

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:22.910
Do you have any flying Pokémon?

00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:26.390
Sure do! Come out, Kairyu!

00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:35.150
What’s with this one?

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:40.410
There, there, there…
Calm down, now…

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:44.730
What a cutie!

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:46.200
And I brought…

00:03:50.210 --> 00:03:52.080
A Spear, huh?

00:03:54.860 --> 00:03:57.130
This one’s mine!

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:03.450
Oh! A Warrgle, huh?

00:04:03.450 --> 00:04:06.210
If you want to cross
the Resort Desert,

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:09.130
then this is by far
the most fun way to do it!

00:04:09.130 --> 00:04:11.020
Counting on you, Warrgle!

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:15.820
See ya! You try it, too!

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:17.680
So cool…

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:19.350
Let’s give it a try!

00:04:19.350 --> 00:04:20.350
Yeah!

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:25.410
We’re so quick!

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:28.200
Spear, go, go!

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:35.750
Don’t let them beat you, Kairyu!
Full speed ahead!

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:45.280
Kairyu?!

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:47.310
Stop!

00:04:53.180 --> 00:04:54.920
That was great!

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:57.980
You don’t have to pretend.
Look!

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:03.660
We made it!
It’s the Ruins of the Titan!

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:07.610
Hey, wait!
Don’t be so hasty!

00:05:07.610 --> 00:05:10.550
You gotta be tired from flying, right?
Take a rest.

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:22.920
Watch out!
It’s Overheat!

00:05:33.760 --> 00:05:37.520
Hihidaruma’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:40.730
Hihidaruma! Blazing Pokémon!
Fire type!

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:44.370
Its internal fire burns at
1,400 degrees,

00:05:44.370 --> 00:05:47.620
making enough power that it can
destroy a dump truck with one punch!

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:52.760
That was pretty surprising,
huh, Pikachu, Hibunny?

00:05:52.760 --> 00:05:54.120
Hello?

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:56.990
Are you two all right?

00:05:57.960 --> 00:05:59.660
The Hitomoshi spoke!

00:05:59.660 --> 00:06:00.840
Of course it didn’t.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:06.620
I’m the chief of
the excavation team!

00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:10.080
Hitomoshi is my excavating partner,
who lights our path!

00:06:12.170 --> 00:06:15.010
I see…
That was really surprising.

00:06:15.010 --> 00:06:18.650
<i>Enchanting</i>, isn’t it?

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:24.320
This area used to be a city long ago.

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:29.570
It’s said that the people created the Titan
to protect the city!

00:06:29.570 --> 00:06:30.810
Awesome!

00:06:30.810 --> 00:06:31.580
Yeah!

00:06:31.580 --> 00:06:36.540
And this is its key!
<i>Enchanting</i>, isn’t it?

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:40.340
I feel like I’ve seen that before,
but I’m not sure…

00:06:40.340 --> 00:06:43.920
Chief! We’ve found
another inscription!

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:45.920
Very well! I’ll be right there.

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:48.060
I feel the call… Twinkle!

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:51.880
The call of something
new and <i>enchanting!</i>

00:06:51.880 --> 00:06:55.690
You two!
Proceed carefully through the ruins!

00:06:55.690 --> 00:06:59.310
There are some <i>enchanting</i>
surprises in store!

00:07:04.220 --> 00:07:05.850
Be careful, Pikachu.

00:07:05.850 --> 00:07:07.400
Don’t rush, either, Hibunny.

00:07:14.540 --> 00:07:15.620
A Meguroco!

00:07:16.050 --> 00:07:20.000
Meguroco! Desert Croc Pokémon!
Ground/Evil type!

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:26.630
They live hidden under hot desert sands
in order to keep their body temperature from dropping!

00:07:32.950 --> 00:07:35.430
Pikachu! Electricity won’t work
on Meguroco!

00:07:36.340 --> 00:07:37.730
Hibunny, use Double Kick!

00:07:45.220 --> 00:07:47.190
Monster Ball, go!

00:07:57.230 --> 00:07:58.290
You did it!

00:07:58.710 --> 00:08:02.290
Meguroco’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:04.910
My second Isshu Pokémon!

00:08:05.800 --> 00:08:10.030
Was this what the chief meant
by “surprises”?

00:08:11.260 --> 00:08:12.490
A Koromori!

00:08:12.490 --> 00:08:14.010
All right! I’ll get that one!

00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:26.340
<i>This</i> is what he meant
by “surprises”!

00:08:26.340 --> 00:08:29.630
Maybe they're warnings to
stay away from the Titan!

00:08:31.340 --> 00:08:33.080
Did you just hear a click?

00:08:33.660 --> 00:08:35.370
Don’t tell me…

00:08:55.640 --> 00:08:59.320
This ruin is way too intense…

00:08:59.320 --> 00:09:01.180
Oh, a Deathmas…

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:03.810
But I’m getting fired up!

00:09:04.360 --> 00:09:07.410
Let’s go, Pikachu!
We’ll race to the Titan!

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:11.990
And he’s getting
all hyped up, as usual…

00:09:11.990 --> 00:09:15.160
Pikachu, watch out for
the surprises!

00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:22.460
Satoshi!

00:09:23.060 --> 00:09:25.130
Asanan! Psychokinesis!

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:31.260
Pull him up!

00:09:35.520 --> 00:09:36.740
Over here, young man!

00:09:36.740 --> 00:09:38.060
It’s you!

00:09:39.280 --> 00:09:40.620
All right…

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:47.780
Oh, it’s you two!

00:09:47.780 --> 00:09:49.270
Thank you.

00:09:49.750 --> 00:09:55.910
I’m Keira! Wherever there’s mystery and adventure,
you’ll find Asanan and I!

00:09:55.910 --> 00:09:57.240
Or something!

00:09:58.190 --> 00:10:04.100
This inscription seems to be
talking about this emblem.

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:11.330
I came because I wanted to find out
what the Titan was, too.

00:10:11.330 --> 00:10:16.180
But you came without any equipment?
Don’t underestimate the ruins!

00:10:16.180 --> 00:10:20.150
So, Keira, the surprises…
I mean…

00:10:20.150 --> 00:10:21.850
The traps didn’t get you
on the way here?

00:10:22.320 --> 00:10:25.350
Of course not! I mean,
they had switches, you know?

00:10:25.750 --> 00:10:26.850
These.

00:10:26.850 --> 00:10:29.150
Oh, yeah…

00:10:29.150 --> 00:10:33.400
If you step on or move these,
the traps will activate.

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:38.730
No!

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:41.970
That’s a switch to a trap!

00:10:41.970 --> 00:10:42.700
Quiet!

00:10:43.530 --> 00:10:44.190
What’s up?

00:10:44.190 --> 00:10:45.790
We didn’t touch anything!

00:10:45.790 --> 00:10:46.720
Shhh!

00:10:57.090 --> 00:10:58.540
Deathkan…

00:10:59.150 --> 00:11:00.600
My third Isshu Pokémon!

00:11:00.600 --> 00:11:01.970
Wait!

00:11:01.970 --> 00:11:03.760
There’s someone inside.

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:06.090
They’ll be turned into mummies!

00:11:06.090 --> 00:11:07.480
Mummies?!

00:11:07.770 --> 00:11:08.570
PocketMonsters

00:11:08.570 --> 00:11:10.210
Pocket Monsters!
PocketMonsters

00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:14.570
PocketMonsters

00:11:14.570 --> 00:11:19.490
. Ghost .
Ground
Golugh
PocketMonsters

00:11:24.490 --> 00:11:25.080
Wait!

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:31.320
Fighting-type moves won’t work
on the Ghost-type Deathkan!

00:11:31.880 --> 00:11:35.340
Leave it to us!
Pikachu! 100,000 Volts!

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:42.100
They’re free!

00:11:43.180 --> 00:11:44.510
Wham!

00:11:50.810 --> 00:11:53.540
Oh, you truly are my savior!

00:11:53.540 --> 00:11:55.570
Thank you! Thank you!
Thank you!

00:11:57.900 --> 00:11:59.940
Satoshi, that’s...

00:11:59.940 --> 00:12:01.370
A blue Koduck!

00:12:01.370 --> 00:12:03.120
I’ve never seen one before!

00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:07.200
How do you do? My name is Colovari!
Isn’t my Koduck adorable?

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:11.370
I want to fill out my Pokémon Index with
nothing but alternate-color Pokémon!

00:12:11.860 --> 00:12:13.190
Only alternate-color ones?

00:12:13.190 --> 00:12:15.500
I have more! Look!

00:12:16.640 --> 00:12:19.410
Whoa! They <i>are</i> all
alternate-color!

00:12:19.410 --> 00:12:22.210
But it’s a pretty empty list…

00:12:22.210 --> 00:12:24.760
I’m just getting started…
There’s more to come!

00:12:24.760 --> 00:12:28.290
Koduck is the first Pokémon
I ever caught!

00:12:28.290 --> 00:12:31.280
Having your first Pokémon be alternate-color…
feels like destiny, doesn’t it?

00:12:31.280 --> 00:12:32.730
So I made up my mind!

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:36.530
I would fill out my Index in a way
nobody has ever done before!

00:12:36.530 --> 00:12:39.150
Alternate-color Pokémon
are really rare, you know.

00:12:39.150 --> 00:12:43.530
Doesn’t matter! No matter how many years
it takes, I will see it done!

00:12:43.530 --> 00:12:47.060
Hey, how’d you know
there was someone in there?

00:12:47.060 --> 00:12:50.300
Because the Deathkan’s bodies
were hanging close to the ground.

00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:55.540
When they’ve swallowed a person,
the weight makes them droop.

00:12:55.540 --> 00:12:57.170
Huh...

00:13:00.450 --> 00:13:02.420
There’s nothing here!

00:13:02.420 --> 00:13:04.680
Wasn’t this supposed to
be the goal?

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:08.440
Perhaps there’s some hidden setup?

00:13:16.770 --> 00:13:18.120
Everyone!

00:13:18.120 --> 00:13:19.200
What’s up?

00:13:20.270 --> 00:13:22.900
See any more of this emblem around?

00:13:23.990 --> 00:13:25.300
Here’s one!

00:13:25.300 --> 00:13:26.200
I found one, too!

00:13:27.610 --> 00:13:29.140
There’s one here, too.

00:13:29.140 --> 00:13:30.660
Five in all…

00:13:31.730 --> 00:13:33.670
There’s five circles, too.

00:13:33.670 --> 00:13:36.340
Satoshi, push the mark!

00:13:37.350 --> 00:13:39.500
But what if another pitfall opens?

00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:42.260
It’s fine! Trust me!

00:13:42.260 --> 00:13:44.630
Let’s give it a try, Satoshi!

00:13:44.630 --> 00:13:46.570
Don’t blame me if
things go wrong!

00:13:50.890 --> 00:13:52.430
It started moving!

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:54.020
Was it a trap after all?!

00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:56.960
No!

00:13:56.960 --> 00:13:58.270
All of you, push them!

00:14:10.800 --> 00:14:14.350
I knew it!
This is the emblem of the ruin!

00:14:15.220 --> 00:14:16.880
Awesome…

00:14:29.050 --> 00:14:32.910
We did it, at last…
That’s the Titan!

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:52.700
Golugh is the Titan?!

00:14:52.700 --> 00:14:54.360
It’s huge!

00:14:54.360 --> 00:15:00.710
Golugh are 2.8 meters tall…
But this one’s easily above 5 meters!

00:15:00.710 --> 00:15:03.710
I deciphered the inscription!

00:15:05.100 --> 00:15:06.650
<i>Enchanting</i>…

00:15:06.650 --> 00:15:09.700
It’s not “<i>Enchanting</i>”!
It’s a Golugh!

00:15:09.700 --> 00:15:10.970
The Titan was a Golugh!

00:15:16.740 --> 00:15:19.160
W-What’s going on?!

00:15:23.090 --> 00:15:25.070
Stop! Stay away!

00:15:25.460 --> 00:15:27.440
This is what the inscription said:

00:15:27.440 --> 00:15:31.570
Golugh was a city defense system
the ancient people created!

00:15:31.570 --> 00:15:33.700
It only awakens to battle.

00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:36.450
It attacks anything in sight!

00:15:37.840 --> 00:15:40.280
Those ancient people were nuts!

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:46.090
Golugh! Golem Pokémon!
Ground/Ghost type!

00:15:46.090 --> 00:15:50.980
Some say that ancient people invented Golugh
to serve as a laborer!

00:15:50.980 --> 00:15:53.460
It follows its master’s orders faithfully!

00:15:56.030 --> 00:15:57.730
How do we…

00:15:57.730 --> 00:16:01.580
They may <i>call</i> it a Titan,
but it’s still a Pokémon!

00:16:01.580 --> 00:16:03.360
Interesting… Let’s battle it!

00:16:03.360 --> 00:16:06.340
Satoshi! Let’s fight a Raid Battle!

00:16:06.340 --> 00:16:07.640
All right, I’m in!

00:16:09.270 --> 00:16:12.120
If you’re doing a Raid,
then I’m joining in!

00:16:12.120 --> 00:16:15.490
Then I will, too!
It’ll be an <i>enchanting</i> catch!

00:16:15.490 --> 00:16:17.780
I think I’ll skip this one…

00:16:18.750 --> 00:16:20.420
Fight with us!

00:16:20.420 --> 00:16:23.130
I’m an alternate-color
Pokémon collector!

00:16:23.130 --> 00:16:27.760
My friend has one of those!
I’ll introduce you!

00:16:27.760 --> 00:16:29.630
I will aid you!

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:31.260
Koduck!

00:16:32.010 --> 00:16:33.760
Let’s do this, Asanan!

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:37.950
I’m counting on you,
Hitomoshi!

00:16:40.240 --> 00:16:42.100
Now things are
really heating up!

00:16:44.610 --> 00:16:46.730
Pikachu!
100,000 Volts!

00:16:52.100 --> 00:16:53.740
H-Huh?

00:16:53.740 --> 00:16:56.070
Hey, hey, calm down!

00:16:56.070 --> 00:16:59.160
Golugh’s a Ground type,
just like Meguroco!

00:16:59.160 --> 00:17:01.120
Oh, right! What a slip-up…

00:17:06.850 --> 00:17:10.180
Hibunny,
it’s got the Ghost type, too,

00:17:10.180 --> 00:17:12.650
so your moves won’t work on it.

00:17:18.390 --> 00:17:20.910
Hibunny! Are you okay?

00:17:22.140 --> 00:17:25.150
Hitomoshi! Fire Spin!

00:17:27.150 --> 00:17:29.570
Asanan! Psycho Shock!

00:17:33.440 --> 00:17:35.530
Koduck!
Hydro Pump!

00:17:45.110 --> 00:17:46.000
So strong…

00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:50.840
Asanan, come back!

00:17:51.320 --> 00:17:53.510
Battling is too hard!

00:17:53.510 --> 00:17:55.590
Pikachu! Iron Tail!

00:18:08.780 --> 00:18:10.550
You okay, Pikachu?!

00:18:12.400 --> 00:18:14.260
Rest up here.

00:18:14.260 --> 00:18:16.160
We still have Kairyu!

00:18:16.160 --> 00:18:17.900
Go, Kairyu!

00:18:23.120 --> 00:18:25.760
Kairyu! Use Dragon Claw!

00:18:30.420 --> 00:18:33.260
Hibunny,
you watch from here!

00:18:33.260 --> 00:18:35.270
Next up, I’ll use Spear!

00:18:36.840 --> 00:18:38.390
Double Needle!

00:18:44.920 --> 00:18:47.110
Spear! Come back!

00:18:47.650 --> 00:18:51.010
Go, Warrgle! Air Slash!

00:18:53.410 --> 00:18:57.360
Lampler, I’m counting on you!
Flame Burst!

00:19:02.680 --> 00:19:03.580
Lampler!

00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:08.380
Well, then I’ll use the new partner
I just caught! Hihidaruma!

00:19:10.670 --> 00:19:12.170
No hard feelings…

00:19:12.170 --> 00:19:13.880
…no matter who catches it!

00:19:21.350 --> 00:19:22.120
No way!

00:19:22.120 --> 00:19:23.310
It transformed?!

00:19:23.310 --> 00:19:24.790
Oh no… It can’t be!

00:19:24.790 --> 00:19:26.370
What?

00:19:26.370 --> 00:19:29.690
This might be the ultimate attack
the inscriptions described!

00:19:30.190 --> 00:19:34.900
Unleashing light from its body,
the Titan would burn all its foes to ashes!

00:19:34.900 --> 00:19:36.360
Burn to ashes?!

00:19:36.360 --> 00:19:39.310
I can see why they’d
call it “Titan”!

00:19:39.310 --> 00:19:42.230
Let’s have Kairyu and Hihidaruma
do a combo attack!

00:19:42.230 --> 00:19:44.080
Before it can fire its move,

00:19:44.080 --> 00:19:45.430
we’ll finish it off with our attack!

00:19:45.430 --> 00:19:46.200
All right!

00:19:46.200 --> 00:19:47.960
Kairyu! Hurricane!

00:19:47.960 --> 00:19:50.750
Hihidaruma! Overheat!

00:20:07.000 --> 00:20:08.730
It’s acting strangely…

00:20:08.730 --> 00:20:11.690
It might not be able to go back to normal
after sustaining all that damage!

00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:14.940
Golugh!

00:20:14.940 --> 00:20:18.820
Sorry for cutting ahead!
Monster Ball, go!

00:20:26.420 --> 00:20:29.960
Golugh’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:20:29.960 --> 00:20:35.590
Oh, I’m so jealous,
but Golugh is yours, Go!

00:20:35.590 --> 00:20:37.690
Go, that was amazing!

00:20:37.690 --> 00:20:38.720
Nice, Go!

00:20:38.720 --> 00:20:41.530
Kairyu’s battling was amazing, too!

00:20:41.530 --> 00:20:43.180
As was your Hihidaruma!

00:20:49.710 --> 00:20:50.600
Oh?

00:20:52.580 --> 00:20:53.720
Is this…?

00:20:55.730 --> 00:20:59.610
This is the ancient city
the Titan was protecting!

00:20:59.610 --> 00:21:02.030
Ruins are <i>enchanting!</i>

00:21:02.030 --> 00:21:05.270
Perhaps I’ll find an alternate-color,
golden Pokémon!

00:21:05.270 --> 00:21:07.870
Adventure! Adventure!

00:21:13.520 --> 00:21:14.920
Hey, Go!

00:21:14.920 --> 00:21:16.420
Shhh!

00:21:24.430 --> 00:21:27.390
They’re kinda like the guardian deities
of Sakuragi Park, yeah?

00:21:28.800 --> 00:21:30.520
So cool!

00:21:31.150 --> 00:21:35.690
The adventure in the Isshu Region ended
with an unexpected Raid Battle!

